  "raw": " The Field made Marshall Field an internationally renowned retailer and it expanded its reach into North America as well. Different companies managed the Field business while Marshal Field traveled to other countries to expand. Marshall Field died in 1899 leaving the world without his empire! Now it belongs to a trust created by his descendants that owns historic Boston buildings -among them, the original shops of Marshall Field & Company.\n\nBlue Jay Foods is one of the largest chicken producers in Massachusetts, with permanent operations at seven facilities across the Commonwealth. The SuperFarm processes over 80 percent of its chicken production through custom-manufactured cleaning equipment (such as hot/cold scrubbers), horizontal and vertical rerendering, local processing, and clean-up services. These basic experiences demonstrate both Blue Jays experience in developing high-quality poultry parts and other products from bird waste, along with cost savings from working with one resource or system rather than several smaller ones (e.g., addressing food wastage opportunities in addition to leading business initiatives for overall",
